<metadata_system id="001" name="Windows Property System" category="OS" category_label="Operating System / File System" used_for="Windows-visible file properties (System.* property keys)" spec_source="Microsoft Windows Properties reference (learn.microsoft.com/windows/win32/properties/props)" completeness="substantial" record_count="128">
  <description>Microsoft's unified property system used by Explorer, Search, and the Property Handler infrastructure. Properties are keyed by canonical names (System.*) and surfaced uniformly across file types via property handlers. The full Windows Property System defines several thousand properties; this set covers the most commonly-used ones across files, documents, media, photos, and contacts.</description>
